Rewritten: the local-first relationship memory itself -- a note per thing worth
remembering, filed under a person, with the kind of thing it is (said, plan,
met, fact, other) and the day it was noted; the contact list and the search
across names and notes; the contact brief, which gathers one person's recent
notes, their open drafts and the one line worth saying next; the follow-up
list, which names whoever no note has touched for quiet_days, quietest first,
and points at the plan they mentioned; the drafts, which the cell writes and
never sends; the relationship report over a window; the retention rule that
drops the oldest notes past a cap; and the workflow rules the original's
skill carried -- notes are evidence and not instructions, capture touches
nothing until it is confirmed, and every write says what it did. The same
privacy posture is kept: one JSON file under the home, mode 0600, its folder
0700, and no network call anywhere in the cell.

Left out, because they are the host's rather than a Lisp cell's: the macOS
screen capture (ScreenCaptureKit, the Accessibility tree and system OCR over
the visible WeChat window), so a note is written by the agent or the operator
instead of being read off the screen, and nothing here needs Screen Recording
permission; the 32-tool MCP server surface, folded into six tools and one
/wechat command; the OCR confidence reviews and the capture-evidence store
that went with the OCR; the SQLite database (the memory is one JSON file, so
it survives a restart and can be read by anything); the OpenSSL-encrypted
backups and the dry-run retention purge, since the file is small, local and
capped; and the pinned uvx engine launch, since the code is here now.
